+        #
+        # USBIsochronousStreamInEndpoint drives `self.stream.ready` from `m.d.comb`, gated by
+        # `tx_stream.ready`, so without this the ULPI transmit path's readiness reaches
+        # `out_fifo.r_en` inside ChannelsToUSBStream combinationally, and from there the FIFO's
+        # level counter. On an ECP5 at 80% occupancy that cone measures 22.11 ns end to end --
+        # 4.79 ns of it pure logic over ~20 LUT levels -- which caps the `usb` domain at ~45 MHz
+        # against a 60 MHz target. Both `w_rdy` and `r_rdy` of SyncFIFOBuffered come off the
+        # level register, so this splits the cone into 17.69 ns and ~4.7 ns.
+        #
+        # Note the endpoint does not stall on `valid` low: in SEND_DATA it asserts
+        # `tx_stream.valid` unconditionally and consumes a byte whenever `tx_stream.ready` fires.
+        # That is safe here only because ChannelsToUSBStream holds `valid` high for the whole
+        # frame, padding with zeros from its FILL state, so this buffer is primed and stays full.
+        m.submodules.usb_in_skid = usb_in_skid = \
